# Text M6.6b must leave British, one entry per line.
#
# Format:  <repo-relative path>::<the exact text to leave alone>
# m6.6b-spelling.py blanks each entry out of the file before converting it, so the
# words inside are invisible to the pass rather than exempt from it.
#
# There is one reason to add a line: the text is an EXAMPLE of a spelling this pass
# removed. A comment explaining that `centreX` became `centerX` has to be able to
# say `centreX`, and documentation of the milestone has to be able to quote what it
# changed. Everything else is a spelling to fix, not a spelling to protect.
#
# Third-party text does NOT belong here; that is FROZEN_FROM and SKIP_PREFIX in the
# tool itself, so a license body cannot be exempted one line at a time by mistake.

tools/m6.6-guard.py::`centreX` as well as "the box centre"
tools/m6.6-scan.py::"the box centre"
tools/m6.6-scan.py::`centreX` on the line below it

# The two M6.6 documents describe the pass by quoting the identifiers it renamed.
docs/M6.6-SWEEP-PLAN.md::(centreX, thumbCentreY, resizeAroundCentre, colour, grey)
docs/M6.6-UNSLOP-TRACKER.md::`centreX`,
docs/M6.6-UNSLOP-TRACKER.md::`centreScreenY`, `thumbCentreY`, `resizeAroundCentre`, `recentre`, plus `colour` and
docs/M6.6-UNSLOP-TRACKER.md::`grey` throughout

# The M6.6b milestone row and MANUAL.md's own account of this pass, which have to be able to
# write the spellings it removed in order to explain what it did.
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::`centreX`, `centreScreenY`, `thumbCentreY`, `resizeAroundCentre`, `recentre`, `ITEM_COLOUR`, `RECENTRE_MARGIN_PX`, `gesture.cancelled()`
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::A blind substring replacement of `centre` also rewrites
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::contains `programme`
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::`centimetres` is one word, not `centi` plus `metres`
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::"the box centre" and structurally never see `centreX` on the line below
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::`"no such colour block: "`
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::back to `centreX` and watching it report MATCHED NOTHING
MANUAL.md::`centre` with `center` also rewrites the test method
MANUAL.md::contains `programme`
MANUAL.md::`resizeAroundCentre` becomes `resize` + `Around` + `Centre`
MANUAL.md::`centimetres` is a single
MANUAL.md::lowercase word, not `centi` plus `metres`
MANUAL.md::that `centreX` became `centerX` has to be able to write `centreX`

# Future.isCancelled is a real Java API name and stays British whatever this pass does.
# The sentence around it names the identifiers that were checked against it.
docs/claude/MILESTONES.md::**All 42 `cancelled` are ours**, not `Future.isCancelled`; `gesture.cancelled()` and `FILE_CANCELLED` are this project's own names.

